WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.266
In two minutes, you will plan a night of lights, and get a driving route.

00:00:04.266 --> 00:00:05.311
We start on the map.

00:00:06.217 --> 00:00:09.503
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.473 --> 00:00:13.905
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.905 --> 00:00:16.404
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.404 --> 00:00:17.754
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.571 --> 00:00:21.939
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:22.636
Tap Allow.

00:00:27.122 --> 00:00:28.653
Choose what you want to see.

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:29.815
Tap the season button.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.598
Tap Thanksgiving and Christmas Lights.

00:00:36.711 --> 00:00:39.304
On a place you want to visit, tap the heart.

00:00:39.304 --> 00:00:39.880
Add three.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:47.747
Tap My night.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:52.354
Your stops are here, in a sensible driving order, with the miles and the time.

00:00:54.422 --> 00:00:56.833
Choose your maps app, and tap Open route.

00:00:56.833 --> 00:00:58.555
Your maps app takes you there.

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:02.977
Tap Share to send your night to a friend.

00:01:04.627 --> 00:01:06.567
Tap the heart on places you like.

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:08.107
My night builds the route.

00:01:08.107 --> 00:01:10.560
Then open it in your maps app, or share it.

00:01:11.959 --> 00:01:14.189
Next up: Weekly lights email.
